messages:    9%|9         | 56/600 [00:12<01:28,  6.17it/s][["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nMeteorologist: The number of tornadoes reported annually has more than doubled since the 1950s. But their actual number has probably not increased. Our ability to find tornadoes has improved, so we' re probably just finding a higher percentage of them than we used to.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which one of the following, if true, provides the most support for the meteorologist's argument?\n# Options:\nA) The annual number of deaths due to tornadoes has increased steadily since the 1950s.\nB) The number of tornadoes hitting major population centers annually has more than doubled since the 1950s.\nC) The geographic range in which tornadoes are most prevalent has remained roughly constant since the 1950s.\nD) The number of large and medium sized tornadoes reported annually has remained roughly constant since the 1950s.", "<think>.\nTo determine which option provides the most support for the meteorologist's argument, we need to analyze each option in relation to the context provided.The context states that the number of tornadoes reported annually has more than doubled since the 1950s, but the actual number has probably not increased due to improved detection capabilities.Let's evaluate each option:.\n\nA) The annual number of deaths due to tornadoes has increased steadily since the 1950s.\n- This option suggests an increase in the actual number of tornadoes, which contradicts the meteorologist's argument that the actual number has not increased.Therefore, this option does not support the meteorologist's argument.\n\nB) The number of tornadoes hitting major population centers annually has more than doubled since the 1950s.\n- This option also suggests an increase in the actual number of tornadoes, which again contradicts the meteorologist's argument.Thus, this option does not support the meteorologist's argument.\n\nC) The geographic range in which tornadoes are most prevalent has remained roughly constant since the 1950s.\nNeither option supports the meteorologist's argument. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
