messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nObligatory alternative action refers to a situation in which the actor has committed an illegal act and caused the result, but the result cannot be avoided even if he abides by the law.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, according to the above definition, which of the following is an optional act of obligation?\n# Options:\nA) When a was driving normally, a pedestrian named wang rushed to a from the sidewalk and wang was injured\nB) B drunk driving, pedestrian wang also drunk, from the sidewalk suddenly rushed to b, wang was injured\nC) C driving speeding, pedestrian wang across the road, c too late to brake, wang hit\nD) D overload driving, pedestrian wang across the road, fortunately, ding emergency brake, did not hit wang', "<think>.\nTo determine which option is an optional act of obligation, we need to analyze each option based on the definition provided.The definition states that an obligatory alternative action refers to a situation where the actor has committed an illegal act and caused the result, but the result cannot be avoided even if he abides by the law.\n\nLet's examine each option:.\n\nA) When a was driving normally, a pedestrian named wang rushed to a from the sidewalk and wang was injured.\n- In this case, there is no illegal act committed by the actor (a).The pedestrian (wang) chose to rush into the road, which is an optional act.Therefore, this does not meet the criteria for an obligatory alternative action.\n\nB) B drunk driving, pedestrian wang also drunk, from the sidewalk suddenly rushed to b, wang was injured.In this scenario, neither the actor (C) nor the pedestrian (wang) are engaging in illegal acts. The result (wang being injured) could have been avoided if they both followed the law. This does not meet the criteria for an obligatory alternative action.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
