messages:   22%|##2       | 135/600 [00:27<01:58,  3.92it/s][["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nWhy are the brain sizes of some primates larger than other animals? The reason is usually considered to be social behavior, that is, primates live in larger and more complex social groups. In order to better handle various social relationships, they Need a bigger brain.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, if which of the following is true, the above point of view can't be questioned?\n# Options:\nA) It is easier to predict the size of the brain through the dietary characteristics of primates rather than the complexity of the community\nB) Some primates such as orangutans usually live alone, but their brains are also large\nC) The size of the cerebral cortex is not directly related to the size of the brain, but it is very important for primate cognition, spatial reasoning ability, etc\nD) Among primates, fruit-eating animals have larger brains than leaf-eating animals. this is because fruits are more dispersed in time and space, and finding fruits is a more complicated task", "<think>.\nTo determine which option can't be questioned based on the given context, let's analyze each option step by step:.\n\nA) It is easier to predict the size of the brain through the dietary characteristics of primates rather than the complexity of the community.\n- This option suggests that the size of the brain can be predicted based on dietary characteristics, which contradicts the context that social behavior is the primary reason for larger brain sizes in primates.Therefore, this option can be questioned.\n\nB) Some primates such as orangutans usually live alone, but their brains are also large.\n- This option states that some primates living alone have large brains, which contradicts the context that social behavior is the primary reason for larger brain sizes in primates.Therefore, this option can be questioned.\n\nThe size of the cerebral cortex is directly related to the size of the brain and is not important for primate cognition, spatial reasoning ability, etc.\n- This option suggests that the size of the cerebral cortex is directly related to the size of the brain, supporting the context that social behavior is the primary reason for larger brain sizes in primates.Therefore, this option cannot be questioned.\n\nD) Among primates, fruit-eating animals have smaller brains than leaf-eating animals.This is because fruits are less dispersed in time and space, and finding fruits is a less complicated task.\n- This option suggests that the size of the brain is not related to the complexity of finding food, which contradicts the context that social behavior is the primary reason for larger brain sizes in primates.Therefore, this option can be questioned\n. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
