messages:  [["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nNative speakers perceive sentences of their own language as sequences of separate words. But this perception is an illusion. This is shown by the fact that travelers who do not know a local language hear an unintelligible, uninterrupted stream of sound, not sentences with distinct words.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which one of the following is an assumption on which the argument depends?\n# Options:\nA) Native speakers' perceptions of their own language are not more accurate than are the perceptions of persons who do not know that language.\nB) Accomplished non-native speakers of a language do not perceive sentences as streams of sound.\nC) It is impossible to understand sentences if they are in fact uninterrupted streams of sound.\nD) People pay less close attention to the way their own language sounds than they do to the way an unfamiliar language sounds.", "<think>.\nTo determine the correct assumption on which the argument depends, let's analyze each option step by step:.\n\nNative speakers' perceptions of their own language are more accurate than the perceptions of persons who do not know that language. This option implies that native speakers have a superior understanding of their language compared to non-native speakers. As a result, this assumption is crucial to the argument's validity.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
