re.\nThis option directly addresses the idea that the city is a way of life and an experience.It suggests that the popularity of a city grows over time, leading to its maturity.This contradicts the context provided, which indicates that the city is not a way of life and that it does not take several years to mature.\n\nA) Small cities have small populations and are quickly matured.\nThis option implies that small cities have small populations and quickly mature, which directly contradicts the idea that the city is a way of life or an experience. It emphasizes the size and speed of maturity of the city rather than the personal experience or the time it takes for maturity.\n\nIn light of the analysis, option B best opposes the given point of view. The context implies that the city is not a way of life or an experience, and option B suggests that the popularity of a city remains stagnant over time, hindering its maturity.\n. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
