messages:  [["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nOur parents pay more and more attention to children's reading. Most parents want their children to read more and read better books. In 2018,70.3 percent of families in one city had the habit of parents reading with their children. The amount of books read by parents and children increased by 1.8 percentage points compared to 2017 and the length of books read also increased compared to last year. But in 2018, the city's children read just 4.72 books per person, down 0.6 percentage points from 2017.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following, if true, best explains the phenomenon?\n# Options:\nA) In recent years, children have a heavy burden of schoolwork and many people want to read extracurricular reading but do not have enough time.\nB) Most parents born in the 1980s and 1990s are highly educated and value reading for their children.\nC) Many children are used to listening to books in parent-child reading, which is not counted in 2018.\nD) Electronic reading by parents on mobile phones and computers has not been taken into account in children's books.", "<think>.\nTo determine which option best explains the phenomenon of children reading just 4.72 books per person in 2018, we need to consider the context provided and analyze each option step by step.\n\nFirst, let's review the context:.\n- Most parents in the city have the habit of reading with their children.\n- The amount of books read by parents and children increased by 1.8 percentage points compared to 2017.\n- The length of books read also increased compared to last year.\n- However, the number of books read by children decreased by 0.6 percentage points from 2017.\n\nNow, let's analyze each option:.\n\nA) In recent years, children have a heavy burden of schoolwork and many people want to read extracurricular reading but do not have enough time.\n- This option suggests that children's reading habits are affected by their schoolwork and lack of time for extracurricular reading.While this could be a factor, it does not directly explain why the number of books read by children decreased.\n\nB) Most parents born in the 1980s and 1990s are highly educated and value reading for their children.\n- This option suggests that the increase in reading habits among parents and children is due to the educational background of the parents.However, it does not explain why the number of books read by children decreased.\n\nThe decrease in the number of books read by children can be attributed to the fact that electronic reading by parents on mobile phones and computers has not been considered in children's books. This explanation may not directly address the decrease in children's book reading, despite the increase in electronic reading by parents.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
