messages:   61%|######1   | 368/600 [05:48<00:47,  4.92it/s][["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nKarl Polanyi said that if the market mechanism is allowed to become the sole guide of the destiny of mankind, its natural environment, and the amount and use of purchasing power, it will lead to the destruction of society. As far as commodities are concerned, labor cannot be arbitrarily driven and used. Even abandon without affecting the individual who happens to be the bearer of this special commodity. That is to say, when disposing of a person's labor, the system always faces the unity of body, psychology and morality under the title of person.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following is the gist of the statement above?\n# Options:\nA) Unregulated markets will destroy society\nB) Labor is a special commodity\nC) The unregulated market lacks moral attributes\nD) Labor cannot be commoditized", "<think>.\nTo determine the gist of the statement, let's break down the context and analyze each option step by step:.\n\n1.The context mentions Karl Polanyi's quote about the dangers of allowing the market mechanism to guide society's destiny.This implies that the market should not be the sole determinant of everything, including the environment and purchasing power.\n\n2.Regulated markets will enhance society - This option contradicts the context, as it highlights the benefits of allowing the market mechanism to guide society's destiny with appropriate regulation. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
