messages:   62%|######1   | 370/600 [05:48<00:46,  4.97it/s][["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nIn recent years, as tourism exploration has become more and more popular by some people, there are more and more rescue operations. Should we charge for the deployment of public resources to rescue tourism explorers who commit intentional adventures? These issues have also become the topic that everyone is most concerned about. The positive side thinks that it should be charged; the opposite side thinks that it should not be charged.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following, if true, cannot support the positive side's point of view?\n# Options:\nA) A rational citizen should be responsible for his own actions; otherwise, it will be unfair to other taxpayers\nB) The establishment of a professional rescue system requires a certain amount of financial support\nC) It is the duty of government departments to rescue people in distress. simple charges can not help adventurers build up a sense of social responsibility\nD) Tourist explorers who illegally enter unsafe areas and waste social resources and taxpayers' money should bear the corresponding expenses", "<think>.\nTo determine which option cannot support the positive side's point of view, let's analyze each option step by step:.\n\nA) A rational citizen should be responsible for his own actions; otherwise, it will be unfair to other taxpayers.\nThis option suggests that tourists should be responsible for their own actions and that charging for rescue operations would be fair.This aligns with the positive side's point of view.\n\nB) The establishment of a professional rescue system requires a certain amount of financial support.\nThis option indicates that there is a need for financial support to establish a professional rescue system.This supports the positive side's point of view as it implies that rescue operations require resources.\n\nC) It is the duty of government departments to rescue people in distress.Simple charges can not help adventurers build up a sense of social responsibility.This option asserts that government departments are not obligated to rescue people in distress and that charging for rescue operations could potentially aid adventurers in developing a sense of social responsibility. This contradicts the positive side's perspective.\n\nB) Responsible adventurers who enter safe areas and utilize social resources and taxpayers' money should not bear any expenses.\nThis option implies that responsible adventurers who use social resources and taxpayers' money in safe areas should not bear any expenses. This contradicts the positive side's point of view by suggesting that adventurers should not be held accountable for their actions.\n\nBased on the analysis, all of the options directly challenge the positive side's point of view.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
