messages:   63%|######3   | 379/600 [05:53<01:30,  2.45it/s][['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nArchaeologists from the University of York and the University of Manchester in England have found the remains of a human house with a history of more than 10,000 years in Starka, North Yorkshire. Dating results show that it is a round wooden hut about 3.5 meters high, which existed in 8500 BC and is at least 500 years earlier than the oldest house previously found in Britain. Archaeologists also found a wooden platform and the trunk of a well-preserved tree nearby. In addition, they also found ornaments of processed antlers, indicating that people at that time already had some ceremonial activities.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the followings, if true, can best support the above point of view?\n# Options:\nA) The wooden platform is the workplace where human beings build small wooden houses.\nB) At that time, the british already had a relatively stable address, rather than the previously thought of unsettled hunters.\nC) Humans are gregarious animals, and there are more wooden houses waiting to be discovered nearby.\nD) Only when ceremonial activities are held will the ornaments of processed antlers appear.', "<think>.\nTo determine which option best supports the point of view presented in the context, let's analyze each option step by step:.\n\nA) The wooden platform is the workplace where human beings build small wooden houses.\n- This option suggests that the wooden platform was used for building houses, which contradicts the idea that the house was already built before the platform was found.Therefore, this option does not support the point of view.\n\nB) At that time, the British already had a relatively stable address, rather than the previously thought of unsettled hunters.\n- This option aligns with the context, which mentions that the house existed for more than 10,000 years and is at least 500 years earlier than the oldest house previously found in Britain.This suggests that the people who lived in the house had a relatively stable address, which supports the point of view.\n\nC) Humans are gregarious animals, and there are more wooden houses waiting to be discovered nearby.\n- This option is speculative and not supported by the context.The context only mentions the discovery of one house, and there is no information about other houses or the gregarious nature of humans.\nCeremonial activities will never result in the appearance of processed antlers' ornaments.\n. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
