plies that the survey did not consider the proportion of motorcycles and car Y in the overall population of vehicles.If the survey only looked at car Y, it might not accurately represent the safety of all vehicles.This could be a potential flaw.\n\nC) The safety of a vehicle might depend on other factors besides how often that vehicle is involved in high-speed crashes resulting in fatalities.This option implies that the insurance agent's reasoning takes into account various factors impacting vehicle safety, including design, maintenance, and driver behavior. Focusing solely on the number of high-speed crashes resulting in fatalities is not the main concern when assessing vehicle safety. This may not indicate a flaw.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
