messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nFor example, X X Group held an anniversary celebration, your mobile phone number won a grand prize of 100000 yuan. this kind of unwise fraudulent text messages on mobile phones still appear again and again even after they have been exposed by the media. Professional swindlers prefer to use shoddy fraudulent text messages rather than design more deceptive and gullible text messages, which only shows that the swindlers are too stupid and unprofessional.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following options, if true, strongly refutes the above conclusion?\n# Options:\nA) A swindler must be smart, otherwise it is impossible to deceive others.\nB) When swindlers cheat, they will try their best not to attract the attention of the police.\nC) If a deception was useless, the swindler would have eliminated it long ago.\nD) Swindlers use such text messages to catch people who may be fooled, and they want to filter out smart people in the first place.', "<think>.\nTo determine which option strongly refutes the conclusion that professional swindlers are too stupid and unprofessional, we need to analyze each option in relation to the given context.Let's break down each option:.\n\nA) A swindler must be smart, otherwise it is impossible to deceive others.\n- This option suggests that swindlers need to be smart to deceive others.However, the context does not provide any information about the intelligence level of swindlers.It only mentions that they prefer shoddy fraudulent text messages, which could imply a lack of sophistication or intelligence.This option does not directly refute the conclusion about the swindlers' intelligence.\n\nB) When swindlers cheat, they will try their best not to attract the attention of the police.\n- This option implies that swindlers are aware of the risks associated with being caught and therefore take steps to avoid detection.However, the context does not mention anything about swindlers' awareness of the risks or their efforts to avoid detection.This option does not directly refute the conclusion about the swindlers' intelligence.\n\nC) If a deception was useless, the swindler would have eliminated it long ago.\n- This option suggests that swindlers would eliminate useless deceptions if they were aware of their ineffectiveness.However, the context does not provide any information about swindlers' awareness of the effectiveness of their deceptions.This option directly refutes the conclusion about the swindlers' intelligence.\n\nD) Swindlers use such text messages to catch people who may be fooled, and they want to filter out smart people in the first place.\n- This option implies that swindlers use deceptive text messages to target individuals who are likely to be deceived, suggesting they are not aware of their targets' intelligence level. This contradicts the notion that swindlers are intelligent and selective in their approach.\n\nBased on the analysis, option D weakens the argument that professional swindlers are intelligent and selective. Therefore, the correct answer is not D.\n</think>.\n<answer>\n. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
