er the faculty their desired salary increase.\n- This option is not necessary for the conclusion to be drawn.The context states that the school board president is aware of the consequences of increasing the faculty's salary, but it does not mention the president's authority to offer the desired salary increase.\n\nC) The faculty of grey county public schools will not be going on strike.This option is necessary for the conclusion to be drawn. If the faculty accepts a package of improved benefits instead of their desired wage increase, the school board would not need to cut any after-school programs to increase the faculty's salary.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
