messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nIf you close all the wrong doors, truth will be shut out.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following is closest to the meaning of the above judgement?\n# Options:\nA) If truth is shut out, it must be that you close all the wrong doors.\nB) Truth can not be shut out unless all the doors of wrong are closed.\nC) If the truth is not shut out, then the door to all wrong must not be closed.\nD) To accept the truth, we must reject wrong.', '<think>.\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, let\'s break down the given statement and analyze each option step by step.\n\nThe given statement is: "If you close all the wrong doors, truth will be shut out.".\n\nThis statement can be rephrased as: "Closing all the wrong doors is necessary for truth to be shut out.".\n\nNow, let\'s analyze each option:.\n\nA) If truth is shut out, it must be that you close all the wrong doors.\nThis option suggests that if truth is shut out, then all the wrong doors must have been closed.However, this is not necessarily true.It could be that truth was shut out due to other factors, such as a lack of effort or resources to close the wrong doors.\n\nB) Truth can not be shut out unless all the doors of wrong are closed.\nThis option suggests that truth can only be shut out if all the wrong doors are closed.This aligns with the original statement, as it implies that closing all the wrong doors is necessary for truth to be shut out.\n\nPlease create an illogical reasoning problem. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
