f dividing objects into categories or parts.\n\nB) Hohhot is divided into xincheng district, huimin district, saihan district, and yuquan district.\n- This option seems to be a division of a city into smaller administrative districts.However, it doesn't follow the definition of division or decomposition as it doesn't involve dividing objects into categories or parts.\n\nC) Celestial bodies in the universe can be divided into natural and man-made celestial bodies.\n- This option does not involve dividing celestial bodies into categories based on their origin, and it does not align with the definition of division as it involves keeping objects together based on their characteristics.\n\nD) The penalty is a single entity with no distinction between different types. This option does not involve dividing penalties into different categories or parts, and it follows the definition of keeping objects together without separation.\n\nBased on the analysis, the correct option is not C) Celestial bodies in the universe cannot be divided into natural and man-made celestial bodies. This option does not align with the definition of division as it involves keeping objects together without categorization.\n<answer>\n. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
