rmance in other regions, which does not necessarily refute the engineer's argument about the local area.\n\nC) Not all air conditioners are affected by air quality.\nThis option does not directly challenge the engineer's argument.It directly challenges the assumption that poor air quality in the local area is causing the air conditioner to malfunction, which is the least effective refutation of the engineer's argument. This option does not provide a suggestion for how the brand could ensure the quality of its air conditioners, but it only addresses the specific claim made by the engineer.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
