ropology, which means this statement contradicts the given information.\n\nB) The proposed area studies department would not duplicate more than 25 percent of the material covered in any existing department other than anthropology.\n- This statement denies that the proposed area studies department would duplicate more than 25 percent of the material covered in any existing department other than anthropology.Since the context only mentions the Anthropology Department, this statement is directly supported by the given information.\n\nB) The field of area studies has more than 50 people per year available for hire.\n- This statement denies that the field of area studies has more than 50 people per year available for hire.However, the context states that the proposed department will be funded if there are more than 50 people per year available for hire in that field.Since the proposed area studies department will be funded, this statement aligns with the given information\n. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
