out a broader issue. In the context, the argument assumes that the local historical society is dominated by people who have a commitment to long-term economic well-being, and therefore, the proposal to demolish the old train station should be rejected. Similarly, option B assumes that beauticians suggest that their customers have their hair cut twice a month, and therefore, one should have their hair cut more than once a month.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
