messages:   96%|#########5| 573/600 [11:02<00:04,  5.81it/s][["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nSelf depletion phenomenon is a phenomenon in which individuals' ability or willingness to conduct voluntary activities decline in the process of long-term work, including the decline in ability or willingness to control the environment, control themselves, make choices and initiate behaviors, and at the same time, job burnout, self depletion but no progress.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, according to the above definition, which of the following is self depletion phenomenon?\n# Options:\nA) Lee did not finish his doctoral thesis and continued to postpone it. as a result, he did not graduate from school for eight years\nB) Chen has worked as a deputy director of the magazine for 20 years, and although he has published some personal works, he has not been promoted\nC) Song mou do sales work for nearly ten years, although he changed four or five companies, but because the performance is average, the income has not changed\nD) Wang has been working as an archive administrator for 15 years. he feels numb to his work and has no desire to change the status quo and get promoted", "<think>.\nTo determine which option represents the self-depletion phenomenon, let's analyze each option based on the definition provided:.\n\n1.**Option A**: Lee did not finish his doctoral thesis and continued to postpone it.As a result, he did not graduate from school for eight years.\n   - This option describes a situation where Lee's ability to complete tasks (in this case, finishing his doctoral thesis) has declined over time due to procrastination.However, it does not specifically mention any decline in his ability to control the environment, make choices, or initiate behaviors.Therefore, this option does not fully align with the definition of self-depletion.\n\n2.**Option B**: Chen has worked as a deputy director of the magazine for 20 years, and although he has published some personal works, he has not been promoted.\n   - This option describes a situation where Chen's ability to advance in his career (promotion) has declined over time.However, it does not specifically mention any decline in his ability to control the environment, make choices, or initiate behaviors.Therefore, this option does not fully align with the definition of self-depletion.\n\n3.**Option C**: Song mou do sales work for nearly ten years, although he changed four or five companies, but because the performance is average, the income has not changed.\nBased on the analysis, the correct answer is: Option C. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
