 are of technology\'s drawbacks.This suggests that the sociologist believes that awareness of technology\'s drawbacks leads to resistance to innovations.\n\n3.Now, let\'s examine the question: "Based on the above information, the claim that the more technologically advanced a society is, the more aware its members are of technology\'s drawbacks plays which one of the following roles in the sociologist\'s argument?".\n\n4.We need to identify which option best represents the role of the claim in the sociologist\'s argument.\n\n5.Option A states that the claim is offered as an explanation of why people\'s resistance to technological innovations is more marked the more technologically advanced the society in which they live is.This aligns with the sociologist\'s explanation provided in the context.Option A states that the claim is a fact supported by the claim that technological innovations have no impact on human relations.This option accurately represents the role of the claim in the sociologist\'s argument.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
