 a large invertebrate is directly proportional to its body length.However, this information is not supported by the given context.The context only mentions that the giant shrimp has more than a dozen rows of teeth, but it does not provide any information about the body length of other large invertebrates.Therefore, this option does not support the speculation.The marine shrimps in the Cambrian period did not have a relatively fixed ratio of teeth and body length.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
